{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And you shall slaughter, etc., as I have commanded you.</b> By way of the plain sense (peshat): as I have commanded you regarding the sacrifices, for we do not find in all the Torah any commandment of slaughter except regarding sacrifices, where it is written (Leviticus 1:5): ״ושחט את בן הבקר״." "<b>And by way of</b> the Midrash (Derash): our Rabbis of blessed memory [said], 'as I have commanded you' — at Sinai, orally, as a halakhah given to Moses from Sinai. This is what they said: this teaches that Moses was commanded concerning the gullet and concerning the windpipe, and concerning the majority of one in a bird and the majority of two in an animal."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:47:56.040997513Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}